nd some verbs are irregular in the Simple Past tense in the affirmative form. They have the same structure in the negative and interrogative forms and Wh/Hw questions.<br>  <br>Regular Verbs form the Past tense by adding -d, -ed or -ied.<br> Irregular Verbs have different endings.<br>  <br>Some Irregular Past tense verbs are:</br>  <br>to see -- saw</br> to do -- did</br> to go -- went</br>  <br>Look at the chart and compare."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Regular Verbs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Irregular Verbs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Affirmative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I watched TV.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I went to the movies.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We didn't watch TV.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I didn't go to the movies.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Interrogative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What did you watch?</br>Did you watch TV?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Where did you go?<br> Did you go to the party?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "How are things?"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a casual greeting to show interest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: <span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: Hi Sara! <span class=\"strong\">Sara</span>: Hi Tom! How are things?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le03ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Use these words to talk about what you did last night."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "last night"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "yesterday evening"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I watched TV last night."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le03ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "evening"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "time of the day before night"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you enjoy your evening?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le03ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "for sure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "of course!"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: <span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: Did you have a good night, Sara? <span class=\"strong\">Sara</span>: Oh, for sure!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le03ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "zombie"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a dead person who appears to be alive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I don't like zombies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le03ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "No way!"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Really? You don't say!"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: No way! Did you enjoy the movie?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le03ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le03ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Interview your partner about what they did last night."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask your partner <span clas